Problem Statement

Companies receive large volumes of customer feedback in French (reviews, support messages, surveys), making it difficult to manually analyze sentiment and identify recurring issues.

Objective

Build an NLP system that automatically classifies the sentiment of French customer feedback and helps identify the main concerns expressed by users.

First Version Scope (V1)
Input: French text (customer reviews)
Output: Sentiment (positive / neutral / negative)
Model: Baseline + transformer comparison

Dataset: "allocine" dataset collected by Théophile Blard 
A large-scale sentiment analysis dataset in French language

The Allociné dataset is a French-language dataset for sentiment analysis. The texts are movie reviews written between 2006 and 2020 by members of the Allociné.fr community for various films. It contains 100k positive and 100k negative reviews divided into train (160k), validation (20k), and test (20k). 
